+# TLS Certificate Verification Policy
+
+In this project's current recorded decision, TLS certificate verification is disabled in development builds as a workaround for development environment constraints; this is explicitly scoped to dev builds only, and production builds must keep certificate verification enabled. No later recorded decision revises or reverses this: the subsequent HTTPS-only policy addresses whether communication uses plaintext HTTP versus HTTPS, not whether TLS certificates are verified, so it does not supersede the certificate-verification exception for development builds.
